1
00:00:07,370 --> 00:00:08,860
A party has 6 pizzas.

2
00:00:08,910 --> 00:00:12,130
Each guest gets 3 eighths of a pizza.

3
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:14,160
How many guests can be served?

4
00:00:14,210 --> 00:00:17,730
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:20,240
Cut every pizza into 8 slices.

6
00:00:20,290 --> 00:00:22,890
6 pizzas make 48 eighths.

7
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:25,180
Each guest takes 3 slices.

8
00:00:25,230 --> 00:00:27,130
48 divided by 3 is 16.

9
00:00:27,180 --> 00:00:30,060
So 16 guests can be served.

10
00:00:30,110 --> 00:00:34,530
Remember: 3 divided by a half asks how many halves are in 3.

11
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:37,460
There are 2 in each whole, so 6.

12
00:00:37,510 --> 00:00:42,700
Dividing by a unit fraction, 1 over d, is the same as multiplying by d.

13
00:00:42,750 --> 00:00:45,130
There are d pieces in each whole.

14
00:00:45,180 --> 00:00:47,750
6 divided by 1 eighth is 48.

15
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:48,490
Your turn.

16
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:50,710
Work out 4 divided by 1 third.

17
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:54,110
Pause the video and try it.

18
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:59,140
There are 3 thirds in each whole, so 4 times 3 is 12.

19
00:00:59,190 --> 00:01:04,230
For 6 divided by 3 eighths, we found 48 eighths, then divided by 3.

20
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:07,570
That is the same as multiplying by 8 thirds.

21
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:10,620
8 thirds is the reciprocal of 3 eighths.

22
00:01:10,670 --> 00:01:13,750
You turn the fraction upside down.

23
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:18,850
Dividing by a fraction less than 1 always gives a bigger answer.

24
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:20,200
Here is the method.

25
00:01:20,250 --> 00:01:23,420
Step 1: write the reciprocal of the fraction.

26
00:01:23,470 --> 00:01:25,400
Turn it upside down.

27
00:01:25,450 --> 00:01:29,690
Step 2: multiply the whole number by the reciprocal.

28
00:01:29,740 --> 00:01:34,420
Step 3: simplify, and write it as a mixed number if needed.

29
00:01:34,470 --> 00:01:35,430
Step 4: check.

30
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:39,750
Dividing by a proper fraction gives a bigger answer.

31
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:42,620
Work out 10 divided by 4 sevenths.

32
00:01:42,670 --> 00:01:45,910
Multiply by the reciprocal, 7 quarters.

33
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:51,430
10 times 7 quarters is 70 quarters, which is 17 and a half.

34
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:52,150
Your turn.

35
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:54,400
Work out 6 divided by 2 thirds.

36
00:01:54,450 --> 00:01:57,390
Pause and work it out.

37
00:01:57,440 --> 00:02:00,600
The reciprocal of 2 thirds is 3 halves.

38
00:02:00,650 --> 00:02:04,610
6 times 3 halves is 18 halves, which is 9.

39
00:02:04,660 --> 00:02:09,050
A 5 litre tub fills bottles that hold 2 thirds of a litre.

40
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:10,740
How many full bottles?

41
00:02:10,790 --> 00:02:15,350
5 times 3 halves is 15 halves, which is 7 and a half.

42
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:17,290
The half bottle is not full.

43
00:02:17,340 --> 00:02:20,070
So the answer is 7 full bottles.

44
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:22,780
Sam works out 8 divided by 2 fifths.

45
00:02:22,830 --> 00:02:25,430
Which line goes wrong first?

46
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:26,590
Line 1 is wrong.

47
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:31,380
You turn over the fraction you are dividing by, which is 2 fifths.

48
00:02:31,430 --> 00:02:32,650
Not the 8.

49
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:37,200
8 times 5 halves is 40 halves, which is 20.

50
00:02:37,250 --> 00:02:43,030
A plumber has a 9 metre pipe and needs pieces 3 quarters of a metre long.

51
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:46,560
9 times 4 thirds is 36 thirds, which is 12.

52
00:02:46,610 --> 00:02:50,550
She can cut 12 pieces with nothing wasted.

53
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:51,850
One last question.

54
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:54,360
What is the reciprocal of 7 ninths?

55
00:02:54,410 --> 00:02:57,700
Pause the video and choose.

56
00:02:57,750 --> 00:02:59,210
Turn it upside down.

57
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:02,850
The reciprocal of 7 ninths is 9 sevenths.

58
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:08,020
To remember: dividing by 1 over d is the same as multiplying by d.

59
00:03:08,070 --> 00:03:13,250
Dividing by a fraction is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal.

60
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:17,490
The answer is bigger than the number you started with.

61
00:03:17,540 --> 00:03:20,960
Think about remainders in real problems.

62
00:03:21,010 --> 00:03:26,150
Great work! Now practise lesson 7.5 on Camday.
